text ixc "</tbody>\n</table></div>\n<h2>How the counts work</h2>\n<p>A pull is one fetch this seed served: a <code>git clone</code> or <code>git fetch</code> over HTTPS, counted from the web server's log, or a <code>rad clone</code> or <code>rad sync</code> over the Radicle network, counted from the node's log. Each project page shows the last 14 days, with distinct hosts and distinct Radicle peers per day. Only counts are kept: <code>tools/tally.om</code> reads the logs on this machine and writes numbers, never an address. Seeding nodes are the Radicle nodes this seed knows to be copying the project, itself included. Machine-readable: <a href=\"stats.tsv\">stats.tsv</a>.</p>\n"
